    {
      "type": "Block",
      "value": "---\nesid: sec-Intl.Locale.prototype.getHourCycles\ndescription: >\n  The region used to look up the hour cycle preference is chosen from the\n  available signals in the correct priority order.\ninfo: |\n  HourCyclesOfLocale ( loc )\n  ...\n  2. Let _preference_ be RegionPreference(_loc_.[[Locale]]).\n  3. Let _region_ be _preference_.[[Region]].\n  4. Let _regionOverride_ be _preference_.[[RegionOverride]].\n  5. If _regionOverride_ is not *undefined* and time data for _regionOverride_\n     are available, then\n    a. Let _lookupRegion_ be _regionOverride_.\n  6. Else,\n    a. Let _lookupRegion_ be _region_.\n  ...\n\n  RegionPreference ( locale )\n  1. Let _region_ be GetLocaleRegion(_locale_).\n  2. If _region_ is *undefined*, then\n    a. Set _region_ to CanonicalUnicodeSubdivision(_locale_, *\"sd\"*).\n    b. If _region_ is *undefined*, then\n      i. Let _maximal_ be the result of the Add Likely Subtags algorithm applied\n         to _locale_. If an error is signaled, set _maximal_ to _locale_.\n      ii. Set _maximal_ to CanonicalizeUnicodeLocaleId(_maximal_).\n      iii. Set _region_ to GetLocaleRegion(_maximal_).\n      iv. If _region_ is *undefined*, then\n        1. Set _region_ to *\"001\"*.\n  3. Let _regionOverride_ be CanonicalUnicodeSubdivision(_locale_, *\"rg\"*).\n  4. Return { [[Region]]: _region_, [[RegionOverride]]: _regionOverride_ }.\nfeatures: [Intl.Locale, Intl.Locale-info]\n---",
      "start": 124,
      "end": 1517
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Together, HourCyclesOfLocale and RegionPreference select the region used to",
      "start": 1519,
      "end": 1597
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " look up the hour cycle preference from the available signals in this priority",
      "start": 1598,
      "end": 1678
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " order (highest first):",
      "start": 1679,
      "end": 1704
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "",
      "start": 1705,
      "end": 1707
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   1. the \"rg\" region override keyword (when time data for it exists)",
      "start": 1708,
      "end": 1779
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   2. the region subtag",
      "start": 1780,
      "end": 1805
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   3. the \"sd\" subdivision keyword",
      "start": 1806,
      "end": 1842
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   4. the region computed by the Add Likely Subtags algorithm",
      "start": 1843,
      "end": 1906
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "   5. the \"001\" (world) region",
      "start": 1907,
      "end": 1939
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "",
      "start": 1940,
      "end": 1942
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Each entry below is a locale that carries the signal for its priority level",
      "start": 1943,
      "end": 2021
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " on top of all lower-priority signals, paired with a locale that names the",
      "start": 2022,
      "end": 2098
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " region that signal must resolve to. The paired locale uses the same base",
      "start": 2099,
      "end": 2174
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " language so that any language-dependent locale data is held constant. For",
      "start": 2175,
      "end": 2251
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " example, \"en-US-u-sd-gbeng-rg-gbzzzz\" carries an \"rg\" override of region \"GB\",",
      "start": 2252,
      "end": 2333
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " a region subtag \"US\", an \"sd\" subdivision in region \"GB\", and a base language",
      "start": 2334,
      "end": 2414
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " \"en\" whose likely region is \"US\"; the \"rg\" override has the highest priority,",
      "start": 2415,
      "end": 2495
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " so the locale must behave like \"en-GB\".",
      "start": 2496,
      "end": 2538
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": "",
      "start": 2539,
      "end": 2541
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " The last entry has no lower-priority signals: the language \"eo\" (Esperanto)",
      "start": 2542,
      "end": 2620
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " has no likely region, so its region falls back to \"001\".",
      "start": 2621,
      "end": 2680
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " For each priority level to be observable, the region it selects must have",
      "start": 3128,
      "end": 3204
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " different hour cycles than the region selected by the next lower level in this",
      "start": 3205,
      "end": 3286
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " implementation; otherwise the test could not tell them apart.",
      "start": 3287,
      "end": 3351
    }
  ],
